.TH SETUID 2
.SH NAME
setuid, setgid \- set user and group ID
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B setuid(uid)
.PP
.B setgid(gid)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The user ID (group ID) of the current process is set to the argument.
Both the effective and the real ID are set.
These calls are only permitted
to the super-user or if the argument is the real ID.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
getuid(2)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Zero is returned if the user (group) ID is set; \-1 is returned otherwise.
.SH ASSEMBLER
(setuid = 23.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
R0 = uid
sys setuid
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 23
AX = uid
int 0Xf1
.fi
.PP
(setgid = 46.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
R0 = gid
sys setgid
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 46
AX = gid
int 0Xf1
.fi
.sp
